Q: RowHeaderTemplateSelector Object Parameter is null A: <p>Voici un style DataGridRowHeader</p>
<pre><code>    &lt;!-- Data Grid row header template --&gt;
    &lt;Style x:Key=&quot;RowSelectorHeader&quot; TargetType=&quot;{x:Type DataGridRowHeader}&quot;&gt;
        &lt;Setter Property=&quot;Width&quot; Value=&quot;35&quot;/&gt;
        &lt;Setter Property=&quot;Height&quot; Value=&quot;25&quot;/&gt;
        &lt;Setter Property=&quot;Template&quot;&gt;
            &lt;Setter.Value&gt;
                &lt;ControlTemplate TargetType=&quot;{x:Type DataGridRowHeader}&quot;&gt;
                    &lt;Border x:Name=&quot;SelectorBorder&quot;
                            BorderBrush=&quot;LightGray&quot;
                            BorderThickness=&quot;2&quot;
                            Background=&quot;Gray&quot;
                            SnapsToDevicePixels=&quot;True&quot;&gt;
                        &lt;ContentPresenter/&gt;
                    &lt;/Border&gt;
                &lt;/ControlTemplate&gt;
            &lt;/Setter.Value&gt;
        &lt;/Setter&gt;
        &lt;Style.Triggers&gt;
            &lt;!--Change la couleur quand la ligne est sélectionnée--&gt;
            &lt;DataTrigger Binding=&quot;{Binding IsSelected, RelativeSource={RelativeSource AncestorType=DataGridRow}}&quot; Value=&quot;True&quot;&gt;
                &lt;Setter Property=&quot;Template&quot;&gt;
                    &lt;Setter.Value&gt;
                        &lt;ControlTemplate TargetType=&quot;{x:Type DataGridRowHeader}&quot;&gt;
                            &lt;Border Padding=&quot;1&quot; 
                                        BorderBrush=&quot;LightGray&quot;
                                        BorderThickness=&quot;1&quot;
                                        Background=&quot;Black&quot;&gt;
                                &lt;ContentPresenter /&gt;
                            &lt;/Border&gt;
                        &lt;/ControlTemplate&gt;
                    &lt;/Setter.Value&gt;
                &lt;/Setter&gt;
            &lt;/DataTrigger&gt;
            &lt;DataTrigger Binding=&quot;{Binding IsMouseOver, RelativeSource={RelativeSource AncestorType=DataGridRow}}&quot; Value=&quot;True&quot;&gt;
                &lt;Setter Property=&quot;Template&quot;&gt;
                    &lt;Setter.Value&gt;
                        &lt;ControlTemplate TargetType=&quot;{x:Type DataGridRowHeader}&quot;&gt;
                            &lt;Border Padding=&quot;1&quot; 
                                        BorderBrush=&quot;Blue&quot;
                                        BorderThickness=&quot;2&quot;
                                        Background=&quot;LightGray&quot;&gt;
                                &lt;ContentPresenter /&gt;
                            &lt;/Border&gt;
                        &lt;/ControlTemplate&gt;
                    &lt;/Setter.Value&gt;
                &lt;/Setter&gt;
            &lt;/DataTrigger&gt;
        &lt;/Style.Triggers&gt;
    &lt;/Style&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: How to reference the top container query with nested CSS containers A: <p>You need to use a CSS variable and register it. I wrote a <a href="https://frontendmasters.com/blog/using-container-query-units-relative-to-an-outer-container/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">detailed article on Frontend Masters</a> about it.</p>
<p>You can see it working in the snippet below where the background is limited to <code>--s</code> on both the inner container and the inner child. <code>--s</code> is set on the inner container to <code>20cqw</code> (relative to the outer container) and registered. Since <code>--s</code> is registered, what gets inherited is its computed value = the computed value of <code>20cqw</code> on the inner container where <code>--s</code> is set (not the concept of 20% of the nearest container width), which is relative to the outer container.</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>@property --s {
    syntax: '&lt;length&gt;';
    initial-value: 0px;
    inherits: true
}

div { display: grid }

.outer-container {
    grid-gap: .5em;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 16em), 1fr));
    container: outer/ size;
    border: dashed 2px #001219;
    padding: .5em;
    min-height: 15em
}

.inner-container {
    --s: 20cqw; /* depends on outer container */
    container: inner/ size;
    border: dotted 2px #9b2226;
    background: 
        repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, #bb3e03 0 5px, #0000 0 1em) 
            0/ var(--s) no-repeat
}

.inner-child {
    /* --s still depends on outer container because it's registered */
    background: 
        linear-gradient(90deg, #0a9396cc var(--s), #0000 0)
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div class="outer-container"&gt;
  &lt;div class="inner-container"&gt;
    &lt;div class="inner-child"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="inner-container"&gt;
    &lt;div class="inner-child"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="inner-container"&gt;
    &lt;div class="inner-child"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="inner-container"&gt;
    &lt;div class="inner-child"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="inner-container"&gt;
    &lt;div class="inner-child"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="inner-container"&gt;
    &lt;div class="inner-child"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
